-- title:
--   §2.1, §3.1–3.2, Assumption 1, Definitions 2.1, 3.1, 3.10, pp. 5–10, 13–14, 22 — coefficients, caps Θ, classes 𝒦 and 𝒦̂, φ±, one- and multi-period solutions, value functions
-- statement:
--   This file fixes the model of the multi-period carbon market of Chassagneux, Chotai and Crisan.
--
--   1. **Coefficients and Assumption 1.** The data are $b:\mathbb R^d\to\mathbb R^d$, $\sigma:\mathbb R^d\to\mathbb R^{d\times d}$ and the emissions rate $\mu:\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$. Assumption 1 holds with constants $L\ge 1$, $l_1,l_2>0$, $1/L\le l_1\le l_2\le L$ when
--   $$|b(p)-b(p')|+|\sigma(p)-\sigma(p')|\le L|p-p'|,\qquad |\mu(p,y)-\mu(p',y')|\le L\big(|p-p'|+|y-y'|\big),$$
--   $y\mapsto\mu(p,y)$ is strictly decreasing for every $p$, and $l_1|y-y'|^2\le (y-y')\big(\mu(p,y')-\mu(p,y)\big)\le l_2|y-y'|^2$.
--   2. **Caps.** $\Lambda\in\Theta$ (Definition 2.1) when $\Gamma(\mathfrak e):=\Lambda(\mathfrak e)-\mathfrak e$ is non-increasing and $\Gamma(\mathfrak e)\to-\infty$ as $\mathfrak e\to+\infty$. A separate predicate records the condition $\Gamma(\mathfrak e)\to+\infty$ as $\mathfrak e\to-\infty$, which is **not** part of Definition 2.1 (see the Formalization Note).
--   3. **Terminal classes.** For $\varphi$ non-decreasing in $e$, $\varphi_-(p,e)=\sup_{e'<e}\varphi(p,e')$ and $\varphi_+(p,e)=\inf_{e'>e}\varphi(p,e')$ (1.1). The class $\mathcal K$ (Definition 3.1) consists of $\varphi:\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R\to[0,1]$ that are $L_\varphi$-Lipschitz in $p$ for some $L_\varphi>0$, non-decreasing in $e$, with $\sup_e\varphi(p,e)=1$ and $\inf_e\varphi(p,e)=0$ for every $p$. The class $\widehat{\mathcal K}$ (Definition 3.10) consists of bounded measurable $\Phi(p,e,\mathfrak e)$ such that $\Phi(\cdot,\cdot,\mathfrak e)\in\mathcal K$ with one Lipschitz constant $L_\Phi$ for all $\mathfrak e$, and $(p,\mathfrak e)\mapsto\Phi(p,e+\mathfrak e,\mathfrak e)$ is in $\mathcal K$ for every $e$.
--   4. **Stochastic basis.** A complete probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mathbb P)$ carrying a standard $d$-dimensional Brownian motion $W$ started at $0$, and $(\mathcal F_t)$ the complete filtration generated by $W$. Times are non-negative reals.
--   5. **Spaces.** $\mathcal S^2(I)$: progressively measurable on $I$ with $\mathbb E[\sup_{t\in I}|X_t|^2]<\infty$; $\mathcal H^2([a,b])$: progressively measurable with $\mathbb E\int_a^b|Z_s|^2\,ds<\infty$.
--   6. **One-period solution** of (3.4)–(3.5) on $[t_0,\tau]$ from $(p,e)$ with terminal function $\varphi$: a tuple $(P,E,Y,Z)\in\mathcal S^{2,d}_c([t_0,\tau])\times\mathcal S^{2,1}_c([t_0,\tau])\times\mathcal S^{2,1}_c([t_0,\tau))\times\mathcal H^{2,d}([t_0,\tau])$ with
--   $$P_t=p+\int_{t_0}^t b(P_s)\,ds+\int_{t_0}^t\sigma(P_s)\,dW_s,\quad E_t=e+\int_{t_0}^t\mu(P_s,Y_s)\,ds,\quad Y_{t_2}=Y_{t_1}+\int_{t_1}^{t_2}rY_s\,ds+\int_{t_1}^{t_2}Z_s\,dW_s,$$
--   for $t_0\le t\le\tau$ and $t_0\le t_1\le t_2<\tau$, and, almost surely, the left limit $Y_{\tau-}$ exists and $\varphi_-(P_\tau,E_\tau)\le Y_{\tau-}\le\varphi_+(P_\tau,E_\tau)$.
--   7. **Agreement** of two solutions: $P,E,Y$ indistinguishable on the stated intervals and $Z=Z'$ $dt\otimes d\mathbb P$-a.e.
--   8. **Value function.** $v^\Phi$ is a value function for $\Phi$ on $[0,\tau)$ when, for every $t_0<\tau$ and $(p,e,\mathfrak e)$, a one-period solution from $(t_0,p,e)$ with terminal function $\Phi(\cdot,\cdot,\mathfrak e)$ exists and every such solution has $Y_{t_0}=v^\Phi(t_0,p,e,\mathfrak e)$ almost surely. For $\varphi\in\mathcal K$ the same is done through the injection (3.45), $\widehat\varphi(p,e,\mathfrak e)=\varphi(p,e)$.
--   9. **The recursion** (3.57)–(3.58): $\Phi^{q,k}(p,e,\mathfrak e)=v^q(T_k,p,e,e)$ if $e<\Lambda_k(\mathfrak e)$ and $1$ otherwise, for $k<q$; $\Phi^{q,q}=\theta$.
--   10. **Multi-period solution.** For a grid $0=T_0<T_1<\dots<T_q=T$ and caps $\Lambda_k$, a solution restarted at $t_0\in[T_{k_0-1},T_{k_0})$ from $(P,E)_{t_0}=(p,e)$ with cap parameter $\mathfrak e$ for period $k_0$ is $(P,E,Y,Z)$ on $[t_0,T]$ with $P,E$ continuous in $\mathcal S^2$, $Y$ càdlàg in $\mathcal S^{2,1}$, $Z\in\mathcal H^{2,d}$, the dynamics (2.4) on every period, $Y_T=0$, and the compliance conditions (2.12) almost surely for every period $k\ge k_0$:
--   $$Y_{T_k-}=Y_{T_k}\ \text{if } E_{T_k}<\Lambda_k(\mathfrak e_k),\qquad Y_{T_k-}=1\ \text{if } E_{T_k}>\Lambda_k(\mathfrak e_k),\qquad Y_{T_k}\le Y_{T_k-}\le 1\ \text{if } E_{T_k}=\Lambda_k(\mathfrak e_k),$$
--   where $\mathfrak e_{k_0}=\mathfrak e$ and $\mathfrak e_k=E_{T_{k-1}}$ for $k>k_0$. The model of the paper is $k_0=1$, $t_0=0$, $\mathfrak e=e$.
--   11. **Decoupling field.** $v$ is a decoupling field when, for each $\mathfrak e$, $(t,p,e)\mapsto v(t,p,e,\mathfrak e)$ is continuous on every $[T_{k-1},T_k)\times\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R$, $v(T,\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)=0$, and every restarted solution satisfies $Y_t=v(t,P_t,E_t,\mathfrak e_k)$ for $t$ in period $k$.
--
--   These objects are shared by every statement of the mission: the one-period singular FBSDE of §3.1, its parametrised version of §3.2, and the linked $q$-period system of Theorem 2.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $P$, $Z$ and $b$ take values in `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)`, $\sigma(p)$ in `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d × Fin d)`, so $|\sigma(p)-\sigma(p')|$ in (2.9) is the Frobenius norm (the page names no norm). Stochastic integrals are coordinatewise Itô integrals (`HasBrownianItoIntegral`) of indicator-cut integrands, with continuous-path versions; that relation requires the integrand to be square-integrable on compact time intervals for every $\omega$, a choice of version on a complete space. Path regularity (continuity, càdlàg) is required almost surely. $\varphi_\pm$ are `sSup`/`sInf` of images, meaningful because every use is for a bounded $\varphi$ in $\mathcal K$ or $\widehat{\mathcal K}$. Every time integral carries its `IntervalIntegrable` hypothesis, and the $\mathcal S^2$/$\mathcal H^2$ norms are `lintegral`s in $[0,\infty]$. Left limits are `Tendsto … (𝓝[<] τ)`; every horizon used is positive. The restart family in item 10 and the predicate $\Gamma\to+\infty$ at $-\infty$ in item 2 are additions explained in the goal theorem's note.
-- source:
--   Chassagneux, Chotai & Crisan, Modelling multi-period carbon markets using singular forward-backward SDEs, arXiv:2008.09044v1, pp. 5–10, 13–14, 22, 25, (1.1), (2.1)–(2.4), (2.9)–(2.12), (3.4)–(3.5), (3.45), (3.57)–(3.58), Definitions 2.1, 3.1, 3.10, Assumption 1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_EthierKurtz_SDEState
import Definitions.Def_EthierKurtz_SDEDiffusion
import Definitions.Def_EthierKurtz_IsStandardBrownian
import Definitions.Def_EthierKurtz_completedBrownianPast
import Definitions.Def_EthierKurtz_HasBrownianItoIntegral

namespace CarbonFBSDE.MultiPeriod

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Set EthierKurtz
open scoped NNReal ENNReal Topology

/-! ### Coefficients, Assumption 1 (pp. 9–10), caps (Definition 2.1, p. 7) -/

/-- The coefficient functions `b : ℝ^d → ℝ^d`, `σ : ℝ^d → ℝ^{d×d}` (entries `(i, j)`) and the
emissions rate `μ : ℝ^d × ℝ → ℝ` of the system (2.4). -/
structure Coeffs (d : ℕ) where
  b : SDEState d → SDEState d
  σ : SDEState d → SDEDiffusion d
  μ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ

/-- Assumption 1 (pp. 9–10) with its three constants `L ≥ 1`, `l1, l2 > 0`,
`1/L ≤ l1 ≤ l2 ≤ L`: (2.9), (2.10), strict decrease of `y ↦ μ(p, y)`, and (2.11).
The norm on `σ(p)` is the Frobenius norm of `SDEDiffusion`. -/
def Assumption1 {d : ℕ} (c : Coeffs d) (L l1 l2 : ℝ) : Prop :=
  1 ≤ L ∧ 0 < l1 ∧ 0 < l2 ∧ 1 / L ≤ l1 ∧ l1 ≤ l2 ∧ l2 ≤ L ∧
  (∀ p p' : SDEState d, ‖c.b p - c.b p'‖ + ‖c.σ p - c.σ p'‖ ≤ L * ‖p - p'‖) ∧
  (∀ (p p' : SDEState d) (y y' : ℝ), |c.μ p y - c.μ p' y'| ≤ L * (‖p - p'‖ + |y - y'|)) ∧
  (∀ p : SDEState d, StrictAnti (c.μ p)) ∧
  (∀ (p : SDEState d) (y y' : ℝ),
    l1 * |y - y'| ^ 2 ≤ (y - y') * (c.μ p y' - c.μ p y) ∧
    (y - y') * (c.μ p y' - c.μ p y) ≤ l2 * |y - y'| ^ 2)

/-- Definition 2.1 (p. 7): `Λ ∈ Θ` iff `Γ(𝔢) := Λ(𝔢) − 𝔢` is monotone decreasing and
`Γ(𝔢) → −∞` as `𝔢 → +∞`. -/
def InTheta (Λ : ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Antitone (fun x => Λ x - x) ∧ Tendsto (fun x => Λ x - x) atTop atBot

/-- ADDED hypothesis (not in the paper): `Γ(𝔢) = Λ(𝔢) − 𝔢 → +∞` as `𝔢 → −∞`. -/
def CapUnbounded (Λ : ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Tendsto (fun x => Λ x - x) atBot atTop

/-! ### Terminal classes (1.1), Definitions 3.1 (p. 13) and 3.10 (p. 22) -/

/-- `φ₋(p, e) = sup_{e' < e} φ(p, e')`, (1.1). Used only for `φ` bounded (classes `K`, `K̂`). -/
noncomputable def lowerVer {d : ℕ} (φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ) (p : SDEState d) (e : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  sSup (φ p '' Iio e)

/-- `φ₊(p, e) = inf_{e' > e} φ(p, e')`, (1.1). Used only for `φ` bounded (classes `K`, `K̂`). -/
noncomputable def upperVer {d : ℕ} (φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ) (p : SDEState d) (e : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  sInf (φ p '' Ioi e)

/-- Definition 3.1: `φ : ℝ^d × ℝ → [0,1]`, `L_φ`-Lipschitz in `p` with `L_φ > 0` (3.1),
non-decreasing in `e` (3.2), with `sup_e φ(p, e) = 1` and `inf_e φ(p, e) = 0` (3.3). -/
def InK {d : ℕ} (φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ) (Lφ : ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ p e, φ p e ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) ∧ 0 < Lφ ∧
  (∀ p p' e, |φ p e - φ p' e| ≤ Lφ * ‖p - p'‖) ∧
  (∀ p, Monotone (φ p)) ∧
  (∀ p, sSup (range (φ p)) = 1) ∧ (∀ p, sInf (range (φ p)) = 0)

/-- Definition 3.10: `Φ` bounded and measurable, `Φ(·,·,𝔢) ∈ K` with one Lipschitz constant
`L_Φ` for all `𝔢` (3.44), and for each `e` the map `(p, 𝔢) ↦ Φ(p, e + 𝔢, 𝔢)` is in `K`. -/
def InKhat {d : ℕ} (Φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (LΦ : ℝ) : Prop :=
  Measurable (fun x : SDEState d × ℝ × ℝ => Φ x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2) ∧
  (∃ M : ℝ, ∀ p e ee, |Φ p e ee| ≤ M) ∧
  (∀ ee, InK (fun p e => Φ p e ee) LΦ) ∧
  (∀ e, ∃ L' : ℝ, InK (fun p ee => Φ p (e + ee) ee) L')

/-! ### The stochastic basis (p. 6) -/

/-- A probability space `(Ω, F, P)` (`Pr`), a `d`-dimensional process `W` and a filtration. -/
structure Basis (d : ℕ) (Ω : Type*) [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] where
  Pr : Measure Ω
  W : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d
  𝓕 : Filtration ℝ≥0 mΩ

/-- p. 6: `Pr` is a complete probability measure, `W` is a standard `d`-dimensional Brownian
motion started at `0`, and `𝓕` is the complete filtration generated by `W`. -/
def Basis.Valid {d : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (B : Basis d Ω) : Prop :=
  IsProbabilityMeasure B.Pr ∧ B.Pr.IsComplete ∧ IsStandardBrownian B.Pr B.W ∧
  ∀ t, B.𝓕 t = completedBrownianPast B.Pr B.W (fun _ => 0) t

variable {d : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω]

/-- `J` is a continuous-path version of the Itô integral `∫_0^· H dW^j`. -/
def IsItoInt (B : Basis d Ω) (j : Fin d) (H J : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ ω, Continuous fun t => J t ω) ∧
  HasBrownianItoIntegral B.Pr (fun t => B.𝓕 t) (fun t ω => B.W t ω j) H J

/-! ### The spaces `S²` and `H²` (pp. 5–6) -/

/-- `X ∈ S²(I)` without the path condition: progressively measurable on `I` (the process cut
to `0` outside `I`) and `E[sup_{t ∈ I} |X_t|²] < ∞`. -/
def InS2 {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] (B : Basis d Ω) (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → E)
    (I : Set ℝ≥0) : Prop :=
  IsStronglyProgressive B.𝓕 (fun t ω => I.indicator (fun s => X s ω) t) ∧
  ∫⁻ ω, (⨆ t ∈ I, ‖X t ω‖ₑ ^ 2) ∂B.Pr < ⊤

/-- `Z ∈ H²([a, b])`: progressively measurable on `[a, b]` and `E[∫_a^b |Z_s|² ds] < ∞`. -/
def InH2 (B : Basis d Ω) (Z : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (a b : ℝ≥0) : Prop :=
  IsStronglyProgressive B.𝓕 (fun t ω => if t ∈ Icc a b then Z t ω else 0) ∧
  ∫⁻ ω, (∫⁻ s in Icc (a : ℝ) b, ‖Z s.toNNReal ω‖ₑ ^ 2) ∂B.Pr < ⊤

/-! ### The forward equations (2.2)–(2.3) and the price equation (2.1) -/

/-- `P` solves `dP = b(P) dt + σ(P) dW` on `[t0, T]` with `P_{t0} = p`, almost surely for all
`t ∈ [t0, T]`, the stochastic integral of entry `(i, j)` being `JP i j`. -/
def SolvesP (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (t0 T : ℝ≥0) (p : SDEState d)
    (P : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) : Prop :=
  ∃ JP : Fin d → Fin d → ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ,
    (∀ i j, IsItoInt B j
      (fun s ω => if t0 < s ∧ s ≤ T then c.σ (P s ω) (i, j) else 0) (JP i j)) ∧
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∀ t ∈ Icc t0 T, ∀ i,
      IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => c.b (P s.toNNReal ω) i) volume (t0 : ℝ) t ∧
      P t ω i = p i + (∫ s in (t0 : ℝ)..t, c.b (P s.toNNReal ω) i) +
        ∑ j, (JP i j t ω - JP i j t0 ω)

/-- `E` solves `dE = μ(P, Y) dt` on `[t0, T]` with `E_{t0} = e`, almost surely for all `t`. -/
def SolvesE (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (t0 T : ℝ≥0) (e : ℝ)
    (P : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (E Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∀ t ∈ Icc t0 T,
    IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => c.μ (P s.toNNReal ω) (Y s.toNNReal ω)) volume (t0 : ℝ) t ∧
    E t ω = e + ∫ s in (t0 : ℝ)..t, c.μ (P s.toNNReal ω) (Y s.toNNReal ω)

/-- The Itô integrals `∫_{t0}^· Z dW^j` of the coordinates of `Z` over `(t0, T]`. -/
def ZIntegrals (B : Basis d Ω) (t0 T : ℝ≥0) (Z : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d)
    (JY : Fin d → ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ j, IsItoInt B j (fun s ω => if t0 < s ∧ s ≤ T then Z s ω j else 0) (JY j)

/-- (2.1) on `[a, b)`: almost surely, for all `a ≤ t1 ≤ t2 < b`,
`Y_{t2} = Y_{t1} + ∫_{t1}^{t2} r Y_s ds + ∫_{t1}^{t2} Z_s dW_s`. -/
def PriceEq (B : Basis d Ω) (r : ℝ) (a b : ℝ≥0) (Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ)
    (JY : Fin d → ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∀ t1 t2 : ℝ≥0, a ≤ t1 → t1 ≤ t2 → t2 < b →
    IntervalIntegrable (fun s : ℝ => Y s.toNNReal ω) volume (t1 : ℝ) t2 ∧
    Y t2 ω = Y t1 ω + (∫ s in (t1 : ℝ)..t2, r * Y s.toNNReal ω) +
      ∑ j, (JY j t2 ω - JY j t1 ω)

/-! ### One-period singular FBSDE (3.4)–(3.5) (Proposition 3.2, p. 14) -/

/-- `(P, E, Y, Z)` solves (3.4) on `[t0, τ]` from `(P, E)_{t0} = (p, e)` with the relaxed
terminal condition (3.5) for `φ`, in the classes `S²_c([t0,τ]) × S²_c([t0,τ]) × S²_c([t0,τ)) ×
H²([t0,τ])`. -/
def IsOnePeriodSol (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (r : ℝ) (φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ)
    (t0 τ : ℝ≥0) (p : SDEState d) (e : ℝ) (P : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (E Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ)
    (Z : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) : Prop :=
  InS2 B P (Icc t0 τ) ∧ InS2 B E (Icc t0 τ) ∧ InS2 B Y (Ico t0 τ) ∧ InH2 B Z t0 τ ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ContinuousOn (fun t => P t ω) (Icc t0 τ) ∧
    ContinuousOn (fun t => E t ω) (Icc t0 τ) ∧ ContinuousOn (fun t => Y t ω) (Ico t0 τ)) ∧
  SolvesP B c t0 τ p P ∧ SolvesE B c t0 τ e P E Y ∧
  (∃ JY, ZIntegrals B t0 τ Z JY ∧ PriceEq B r t0 τ Y JY) ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∃ ℓ : ℝ, Tendsto (fun t => Y t ω) (𝓝[<] τ) (𝓝 ℓ) ∧
    lowerVer φ (P τ ω) (E τ ω) ≤ ℓ ∧ ℓ ≤ upperVer φ (P τ ω) (E τ ω))

/-- Two solutions agree: `P, E` indistinguishable on `IPE`, `Y` indistinguishable on `IY`,
and `Z = Z'` `dt ⊗ dℙ`-a.e. on `[a, b]`. -/
def SolAgree (B : Basis d Ω) (IPE IY : Set ℝ≥0) (a b : ℝ≥0)
    (P : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (E Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (Z : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d)
    (P' : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (E' Y' : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (Z' : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) : Prop :=
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, (∀ t ∈ IPE, P t ω = P' t ω ∧ E t ω = E' t ω) ∧ (∀ t ∈ IY, Y t ω = Y' t ω)) ∧
  ∫⁻ ω, (∫⁻ s in Icc (a : ℝ) b, ‖Z s.toNNReal ω - Z' s.toNNReal ω‖ₑ ^ 2) ∂B.Pr = 0

/-- `v^Φ(t0, p, e, 𝔢) = Y^{t0,p,e,𝔢}_{t0}` (Corollary 3.12): for every `t0 < τ` and
`(p, e, 𝔢)`, a solution of (3.4)–(3.5) with terminal condition `Φ(·,·,𝔢)` exists, and every
such solution has `Y_{t0} = v(t0, p, e, 𝔢)` almost surely. -/
def IsValueFn (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (r : ℝ) (Φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (τ : ℝ≥0) (v : ℝ≥0 → SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t0 < τ, ∀ (p : SDEState d) (e ee : ℝ),
    (∃ P E Y Z, IsOnePeriodSol B c r (fun p e => Φ p e ee) t0 τ p e P E Y Z) ∧
    ∀ P E Y Z, IsOnePeriodSol B c r (fun p e => Φ p e ee) t0 τ p e P E Y Z →
      Y t0 =ᵐ[B.Pr] fun _ => v t0 p e ee

/-- `v(t0, p, e) = Y^{t0,p,e}_{t0}` (Proposition 3.2): the case of a terminal `φ ∈ K`, through
the injection (3.45). -/
def IsValueFn₀ (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (r : ℝ) (φ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ)
    (τ : ℝ≥0) (v : ℝ≥0 → SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  IsValueFn B c r (fun p e _ => φ p e) τ (fun t p e _ => v t p e)

/-! ### The multi-period model (Theorem 2.3, p. 10) and the recursion (3.57)–(3.58) -/

/-- (3.57)–(3.58): `Φ^{q,k}(p, e, 𝔢) = v^q(T_k, p, e, e)` if `e < Λ_k(𝔢)` and `1` otherwise,
for `k < q`; `Φ^{q,q} = θ`. -/
noncomputable def PhiQK (vq : ℝ≥0 → SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (θ : SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (Λ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ) (Tg : ℕ → ℝ≥0) (q k : ℕ) (p : SDEState d) (e ee : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  if k < q then (if e < Λ k ee then vq (Tg k) p e e else 1) else θ p e ee

/-- The cap parameter of period `k` for a run restarted in period `k0` with parameter `𝔢`:
`𝔢` in period `k0`, and `E_{T_{k−1}}` afterwards. -/
def capArg (Tg : ℕ → ℝ≥0) (k0 : ℕ) (ee : ℝ) (E : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (k : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  if k = k0 then ee else E (Tg (k - 1)) ω

/-- The `q`-period system of Theorem 2.3 restarted at `t0 ∈ [T_{k0−1}, T_{k0})` from
`(P, E)_{t0} = (p, e)` with cap parameter `𝔢` for period `k0` (the time-0 model is
`k0 = 1, t0 = 0, 𝔢 = e`), on `[t0, T]`, `T = T_q`: the classes `S²_c`, `S²_c`, càdlàg `S²`,
`H²`; the dynamics (2.4) on each period; `Y_T = 0`; and the compliance conditions (2.12). -/
def IsMultiSol (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (r : ℝ) (q : ℕ) (Tg : ℕ → ℝ≥0)
    (Λ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ) (k0 : ℕ) (t0 : ℝ≥0) (p : SDEState d) (e ee : ℝ)
    (P : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) (E Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (Z : ℝ≥0 → Ω → SDEState d) : Prop :=
  InS2 B P (Icc t0 (Tg q)) ∧ InS2 B E (Icc t0 (Tg q)) ∧ InS2 B Y (Icc t0 (Tg q)) ∧
  InH2 B Z t0 (Tg q) ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ContinuousOn (fun t => P t ω) (Icc t0 (Tg q)) ∧
    ContinuousOn (fun t => E t ω) (Icc t0 (Tg q)) ∧
    (∀ t ∈ Ico t0 (Tg q), ContinuousWithinAt (fun s => Y s ω) (Ici t) t) ∧
    (∀ t ∈ Ioc t0 (Tg q), ∃ ℓ : ℝ, Tendsto (fun s => Y s ω) (𝓝[<] t) (𝓝 ℓ))) ∧
  SolvesP B c t0 (Tg q) p P ∧ SolvesE B c t0 (Tg q) e P E Y ∧
  (∃ JY, ZIntegrals B t0 (Tg q) Z JY ∧
    ∀ k, k0 ≤ k → k ≤ q → PriceEq B r (max t0 (Tg (k - 1))) (Tg k) Y JY) ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, Y (Tg q) ω = 0) ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∀ k, k0 ≤ k → k ≤ q →
    (E (Tg k) ω < Λ k (capArg Tg k0 ee E k ω) →
      Tendsto (fun t => Y t ω) (𝓝[<] (Tg k)) (𝓝 (Y (Tg k) ω))) ∧
    (Λ k (capArg Tg k0 ee E k ω) < E (Tg k) ω →
      Tendsto (fun t => Y t ω) (𝓝[<] (Tg k)) (𝓝 1)) ∧
    (E (Tg k) ω = Λ k (capArg Tg k0 ee E k ω) →
      ∃ ℓ : ℝ, Tendsto (fun t => Y t ω) (𝓝[<] (Tg k)) (𝓝 ℓ) ∧ Y (Tg k) ω ≤ ℓ ∧ ℓ ≤ 1))

/-- A decoupling field of the `q`-period model (Theorem 2.3): for each `𝔢`,
`(t, p, e) ↦ v(t, p, e, 𝔢)` is continuous on every `[T_{k−1}, T_k) × ℝ^d × ℝ`;
`v(T, ·, ·, ·) = 0`; and every restarted solution satisfies
`Y_t = v(t, P_t, E_t, E_{T_{k−1}})` on each period (with `𝔢` in the restart period). -/
def IsDecField (B : Basis d Ω) (c : Coeffs d) (r : ℝ) (q : ℕ) (Tg : ℕ → ℝ≥0)
    (Λ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0 → SDEState d → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ ee : ℝ, ∀ k, 1 ≤ k → k ≤ q →
    ContinuousOn (fun x : ℝ≥0 × SDEState d × ℝ => v x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2 ee)
      (Ico (Tg (k - 1)) (Tg k) ×ˢ univ)) ∧
  (∀ p e ee, v (Tg q) p e ee = 0) ∧
  (∀ k0, 1 ≤ k0 → k0 ≤ q → ∀ t0 ∈ Ico (Tg (k0 - 1)) (Tg k0), ∀ p e ee P E Y Z,
    IsMultiSol B c r q Tg Λ k0 t0 p e ee P E Y Z → ∀ k, k0 ≤ k → k ≤ q →
      ∀ᵐ ω ∂B.Pr, ∀ t ∈ Ico (max t0 (Tg (k - 1))) (Tg k),
        Y t ω = v t (P t ω) (E t ω) (capArg Tg k0 ee E k ω))

end CarbonFBSDE.MultiPeriod


